          "text": "Right external ear lesion"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 6–7 mm firm, tender, dome-shaped nodule on the helix/upper antihelix, with superficial central erosion and slight scale/crust, mild surrounding erythema, and very focal tenderness to light pressure. No fluctuance or warmth. No obvious rolled edge or pearly lesion, but crust partly obscures the lesion."
